(                                                     _Toulon, 1 August._) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Alas! Several hours have passed, and I find that all is not well. The) Tj T*
(vessels of the ?naval army? have their staffs of officers completed,) Tj T*
(and from hour to hour await the order to put to sea. I was assigned to) Tj T*
(the _Waldeck-Rousseau_. At another time I should have been proud to be) Tj T*
(a part of this splendid vessel. But she is not prepared to leave port.) Tj T*
(In an accident at sea some months ago, she ripped herself open on the) Tj T*
(shoals of the Gulf of Juan. The healing of great ships is a tedious) Tj T*
(affair, and in a repair basin the engineers are still treating her) Tj T*
(gaping wounds. In reply to my anxious questions, I am told:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(?The workmen are busy on her day and night. In six weeks she will take) Tj T*
(the water again.?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Six weeks! And the other night on the train I saw myself already at) Tj T*
(sea, my vessel en route for her assigned zone. And now I must be) Tj T*
(satisfied with a cruiser that will not stir for six weeks!) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(                                                             _2 August._) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(We lived in an atmosphere heated by the sun of Provence. Arriving from) Tj T*
(Paris as I did, I was questioned. Circles formed, strangers consulted) Tj T*
(me. In vain did I relate what I had seen in the North, describe my) Tj T*
(journey on the railway; these listeners only half believed me. In the) Tj T*
(climate of Provence care disappears; my questioners shook their heads.) Tj T*
(One regretted his ruined vacation; another doubted my testimony; some) Tj T*
(of them invoked the prudence of the Powers, and concluded:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(?Everything will end in a ?Congress of Algeciras.??) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Far removed from the vivid Parisian energy, I felt myself overcome by) Tj T*
(the enervation of Provence. The whole drama of the week took on the) Tj T*
(guise of nightmare. I was annoyed that the great convulsion, ordered by) Tj T*
(Fate, seemed once more delayed by man. I reproached my prudent friends) Tj T*
(for not taking their part in it. Before them the curtain of an epic) Tj T*
(drama was already rising, and they were not hailing with enthusiastic) Tj T*
(acclaim the opening of the spectacle. Their mediocre souls were merely) Tj T*
(taking up again the thread of their daily preoccupations!) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(       *       *       *       *       *) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Towards two o?clock I cross the threshold of the arsenal gate, to pay) Tj T*
(the _Waldeck-Rousseau_ my visit of embarkation. The sky is pouring) Tj T*
(down an avalanche of dusty heat. In such an oven no one can think) Tj T*
(vigorously. Sprawled against the walls, the arsenal workers are mopping) Tj T*
(their faces and chests, and, at the end of their tether, are drinking) Tj T*
(greedily at the roadside bars. Several officers, handkerchiefs in hand,) Tj T*
(are walking along the rows of plane-trees.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The commander of the _Waldeck-Rousseau_ receives me:) Tj T*
ET
