BT /F1 10 Tf 54 738 Td 13 TL
(legends of the sea tell of many a patient cruiser that has rarely been) Tj T*
(rewarded by a battle.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The transports have to carry to France our troops from North Africa. To) Tj T*
(the ?naval army? belongs the duty of protecting these lives. No one can) Tj T*
(tell whether or not this enterprise will be successful. Let a single) Tj T*
(transport fail the summons, and a deluge of sarcasm will fall upon the) Tj T*
(fleet of war! Let sharpshooters and Algerian cavalry within fifteen) Tj T*
(days show their mettle in the valleys of the Vosges, and who will give) Tj T*
(thanks to those who had protected their dangerous voyage? No matter!) Tj T*
(France has distributed the tasks among her children. To the fighters on) Tj T*
(the frontier falls the honor of crushing the Germans; to the sailors,) Tj T*
(the silent guard of the sea.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Perhaps, however, these too will not be denied the glory of battle. At) Tj T*
(the foot of the Adriatic, Austria maintains a fleet that without doubt) Tj T*
(will try to rob us of our empire of the Mediterranean. To release her) Tj T*
(shores she will offer us a naval engagement. The fleet of France will) Tj T*
(prove itself no less worthy than the army; and its deeds, less decisive) Tj T*
(than those of Alsace and of Flanders, will yet prove that the flag) Tj T*
(which flaps at the stern of her ships is without stain.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Au Revoir!) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(                                        _Eve of departure, 5 September._) Tj T*
() Tj T*
