(water, and the work continues. Exhausted by past watches, the crews) Tj T*
(work through this night without losing a second, and find means to) Tj T*
(stow neatly the sacks which will be of no use to them. No matter which) Tj T*
(destroyers and cargo-boats take part, the same business goes on at the) Tj T*
(wharves of Antivari and Medua every three or four nights.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(While this is going on, the destroyers maintain a defense at the) Tj T*
(opening of the bays. The hearts of the men are anxious when they hear) Tj T*
(the fall and see the bursting of the bombs over their toiling friends.) Tj T*
(But their own turn is not long delayed. Before returning to Cattaro the) Tj T*
(airmen do not hesitate to drop their visiting cards on the sentinel) Tj T*
(squadron. But for fear of betraying their position, the latter do not) Tj T*
(reply. At their post on the sea, wiping the spray from their faces, the) Tj T*
(sailors hear the descent of the bombs, screaming in the north wind, and) Tj T*
(keep their spirits equally high whether the shells touch or miss the) Tj T*
