(                                                           _9 February._) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Long hours flow away. The January nights seem eternal when one has) Tj T*
(to live them wide awake. But at last the sky pales in the East, the) Tj T*
(lights of Cattaro sink into the grayness and a sharper cold revives the) Tj T*
(watchers a little. It is dawn.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Empty or not, the cargo-boat casts off its hawsers, and as clumsily as) Tj T*
(it entered the night before, it leaves in the morning. On the wharf) Tj T*
(are heaped the supplies for Montenegro; more will be brought in a few) Tj T*
(days. The stevedores go back to the destroyers, and exchange their) Tj T*
(night?s fatigue for that of the engines and the work of navigating the) Tj T*
(ship. The procession forms again in the mist, and goes down the coast) Tj T*
(of Albania in good shape. Without ballast, the cargo-boat dances in) Tj T*
(the midst of the convoys like a cork. At a great distance the cruisers) Tj T*
(continue their proud vigil until all this little company is out of) Tj T*
(harm?s way. Then they feed their fires, stretch their legs, and limber) Tj T*
(up with a little gallop as far as their Ionian sectors.) Tj T*
