(Or else between sunrise and twilight, they coal in some hidden bay.) Tj T*
(And if chance favors them, they receive letters, and bundles of papers) Tj T*
(which have wandered in pursuit of them over the vast sea. Although it) Tj T*
(has left France so many weeks ago, and is already old, and made stale) Tj T*
(by events, the news is read and commented upon with passion.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The sailors are not turned aside from the great drama by any mediocre) Tj T*
(or banal concerns. Among all the people of the world, it is they who) Tj T*
(vibrate most strongly to all the joys and troubles of France. Their) Tj T*
(clear vision, free from passion, judges calmly the conflict of the) Tj T*
(two parties. Better than anyone, thanks to the patience of their) Tj T*
(pilgrimages, they discern in the future the reasons for victory and the) Tj T*
