() Tj T*
(Bent on their secret task, they do not heed the dazzlement of) Tj T*
(victories. They know that their collaboration, decisive as it is, will) Tj T*
(be effaced by the future prowess of the soldiers. The gunfire, the) Tj T*
(charges, the final drama for which the land will be the theater, will) Tj T*
(relegate their silent labor to oblivion. But to overthrow Germany both) Tj T*
(will be needed, and the glorious army can hold out a grateful hand to) Tj T*
(the Navy.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Already our fleets are closing the doors of the world upon our) Tj T*
(enemies, and keeping them wide open for the resources that will feed) Tj T*
(our victory. As yet it is nothing; but hour by hour we forge a new) Tj T*
(lock. When Germany and her allies, foaming with rage in the prison) Tj T*
(to which our ships are the bars, suffer the tortures of famine; when) Tj T*
(the one hundred and ten millions of Germans, howling at death?s door,) Tj T*
(demand pity, and beg a bit of bread, when this menagerie tears itself) Tj T*
(to pieces in the struggle for food; when revolt, insurrection, and) Tj T*
(the frenzy of civil war shake to its foundations this manufactory) Tj T*
(of murder; then, Russia, England and France will let loose their) Tj T*
(bulldogs and their tamers. From their bridges the marines will hear) Tj T*
(the footsteps of the soldiers? charge and the barkings of their 75?s.) Tj T*
(Their hearts will leap with joy, and, gazing at the sea, the companion) Tj T*
(of evil days and luminous sunrises, they will say to her: ?It is we two) Tj T*
(together who have made it possible for all this to happen.?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Why does my vision wander to those happy days, our recompense? Is) Tj T*
(it because of the contrasting melancholy of winter? Or else, have I) Tj T*
(not been conducted thither by a natural path, through the letters of) Tj T*
(comrades, the illustrious marine fusiliers in Belgium? Since their) Tj T*
(wounds have got better through hospital treatment and convalescence,) Tj T*
(they have commenced writing again. Nearly all my friends over there are) Tj T*
(dead. Those who remain describe in simple language the trip to Antwerp,) Tj T*
(the return in the horror of the conflict, the resistance so savage) Tj T*
(that our enemies will never acknowledge that it was this handful of) Tj T*
(brave men who blocked their rush. History will reward these officers,) Tj T*
(these sailor-soldiers whom we knew on the deck of the men-of-war. Where) Tj T*
(they have been, we should all like to have fought. The entire ?naval) Tj T*
(army? is jealous of this naval brigade. Exiled from the sea, they) Tj T*
