(to dream those dreams one never forgets.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Malta: First pilgrimage of the new crusade. The battleships and) Tj T*
(cruisers, the drag-nets and dredgers get their second wind here before) Tj T*
(sailing for the East, for Constantinople. They go there to take part in) Tj T*
(epic conflicts, and retake from the Osmanlis the city of the Bosphorus,) Tj T*
(which for five hundred years has awaited its deliverance. Regiments,) Tj T*
(batteries and squads accompany them, crowded on the transports and) Tj T*
(eager for victory. May the men who are preparing this great enterprise,) Tj T*
(this terrible enterprise, measure well its obstacles, and be able to) Tj T*
(obviate them!) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Malta, paradise of the vagabond weary of wandering, light fragrances,) Tj T*
