(above us.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A few living things distract our melancholy. Young porpoises, with) Tj T*
(silver bellies and slender snouts, play around the hull, lashing the) Tj T*
(water as if with thongs of whipcord, falling back with a gleaming) Tj T*
(graceful movement. The old porpoises, mere dignified, follow patiently) Tj T*
(their continual leapings, sewing the cloth of the sea with an invisible) Tj T*
(thread; each one of their stitches on this blue material leaves a) Tj T*
(streak of foam.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(When these playful fish pass at a short distance from us, they are) Tj T*
(amusing. But what frights their more distant tracks through the water) Tj T*
(have given the officers of the watch! On an empty and shining sea,) Tj T*
(the silver trail of a porpoise looks too much like the volute of a) Tj T*
(periscope.... And the periscopes are prowling about.... The fine days) Tj T*
