() Tj T*
(Several times at twilight one of the cruisers has seen rising, far) Tj T*
(away, the kiosk and shell of a submarine, coming to the surface for) Tj T*
(the night. The cruiser has rushed upon the enemy, but in the splendid) Tj T*
(evening this fish of steel has filled its reservoirs again and quietly) Tj T*
(submerged. The red of the sky gives place to purple, and the purple to) Tj T*
(violet, and the violet to black, to darkness. The cruiser in pursuit) Tj T*
(has informed the ?naval army? of the encounter. We know she is not) Tj T*
(mistaken, but the other ships, patrolling in the south, treat us as) Tj T*
(visionaries.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Visionaries indeed! If only we were! We should not then experience,) Tj T*
(during our watch, these sudden heart failures, and the nights of the) Tj T*
(watch would not be riddled with these useless agonies. Each day the) Tj T*
(crews become more apprehensive of some fatal surprise, and no one) Tj T*
(is indifferent on board except the animals who dwell with us. Happy) Tj T*
(beasts! Nature has freed them from forebodings.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Our cats, lazy and coquettish, choose a couch on the warm deck in the) Tj T*
(sun, and roll themselves up in a ball, with their nose resting on their) Tj T*
(furry paws, their green eyes half closed; or else they stretch out) Tj T*
