() Tj T*
(They are happier than we, for they are not preoccupied with their fate,) Tj T*
(all the winds that pass are favorable to their wings. Carelessness is) Tj T*
(their daily bread. They never ask the reasons for their pilgrimages,) Tj T*
(and do not guess that their lives might be more useful. We envy their) Tj T*
(spirit and their empty heads. How many times have we not wished to kill) Tj T*
