(?She was wrong. We shall see to-morrow.?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(I go down to dinner. On my chair Jimmino, crouched like a sphinx, is) Tj T*
(waiting for bits from my meal. Our assembly is not very noisy. We) Tj T*
(comment upon the end of the day, and the doctor receives placidly) Tj T*
(the usual pleasantries. The conversation turns listlessly on Turkish) Tj T*
(affairs. Why is there no animation? The officers who are going to) Tj T*
(take the watch rise to put on their uniforms for the night. We greet) Tj T*
(them in the familiar way as they pass out. ?A good watch to you, old) Tj T*
(man! Keep your eyes open!? ?Don?t delay us!? ?You know I?m taking the) Tj T*
(Paris express this evening.? ?If you see a submarine try not to waken) Tj T*
(me.? ?And then,? I added, ?let me know if there is a message from the) Tj T*
(_Gambetta_.?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(?Why??) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(?She has not spoken for nearly twenty-four hours.?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(?The deuce!? murmured the assembly. ?What has happened to her??) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The game tables are set up, for dominoes, chess, bridge; the smokers) Tj T*
(light their pipes; the readers open their paper; others stretch out on) Tj T*
(the cushions. Interpretations are offered concerning the silence of the) Tj T*
(_Gambetta_.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(?Accident to the wireless....?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(?She had nothing to say....?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(?She ought to have signaled her daily position....?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(?She should have replied when she was called....?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(?We shall see to-morrow...!?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The cards fall, the dominoes grate, the newspapers crackle, and the) Tj T*
(pipes pull. All in this little world are silent, absorbed in their) Tj T*
(game, their reading or their reveries. But it is appearance only.) Tj T*
(Yesterday afternoon we talked with the _Gambetta_; last night she) Tj T*
(cruised in the sector where we were to go. For twenty-four hours she) Tj T*
ET
