stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 738 Td 13 TL
(has been silent. In the cards, in the papers, and the smoke from the) Tj T*
(pipes, each one of us reads these disquieting thoughts. But no one) Tj T*
(speaks of it. I go to bed, for I have to take the watch again in the) Tj T*
(middle of the night.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Jimmino trots behind me, installs himself near the pillow, and sleeps) Tj T*
(with a dreamless slumber. But I await through the long hours some news) Tj T*
(of the _Gambetta_. Eyes closed or open, I cannot escape being haunted) Tj T*
(by her. All my comrades tell me they have passed a sleepless night.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In the shadow I go up to take the watch. My predecessor repeats the) Tj T*
(sacred phrases. I interrupt him:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(?But the _Gambetta_??) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(?Nothing.?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(?What do you think of it??) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(?Nothing.?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(?Do you believe that...??) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(I dare not finish. He dares not answer, but disappears in the darkness.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(I fix my eyes on this treacherous sea which never gives up its secrets.) Tj T*
(An anguish with iron fingers presses my heart. There is no more doubt) Tj T*
(of it, death has passed over one of our brothers. Each hour that slips) Tj T*
(by proves the magnitude of the disaster, and if no news ever reaches) Tj T*
(us, it will be because all at one stroke eight hundred men will) Tj T*
(have plunged into the sea. Leaning on the rail, I stroke the metal) Tj T*
(mechanically, and the wood and canvas which meet my hand. I enjoy) Tj T*
(feeling the good cruiser, alive and in motion, quivering under me.) Tj T*
(I realize how much I love her, and it seems to me, that in order to) Tj T*
(pierce the darkness, my eyes take on the acuteness of a father?s who) Tj T*
(scans the face of a child of his that is menaced by death.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A little later our wireless operator sends me a bundle of messages.) Tj T*
(With nervous fingers the ensign translator turns over his codes and) Tj T*
(dictionaries in order to transform these ciphers into French. Each) Tj T*
(minute I go to his shoulder to read the line, or the half-line, or the) Tj T*
(word he has transcribed. Heavens! How long it takes to spell out the) Tj T*
(horror!) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(       *       *       *       *       *) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It happened yesterday evening, during that fatal watch which I found) Tj T*
(so beautiful. The moon was quite round; the sea was transparent, and) Tj T*
(I saw nothing on it. Like me the officers on watch on the _Gambetta_) Tj T*
(were weary of their useless vigil; at the end of their route they saw) Tj T*
(the gleam of the lighthouse at Santa Maria di Leuca. In the distance) Tj T*
(passed the shadows which I should have seen if the _Waldeck-Rousseau_) Tj T*
ET
