stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 738 Td 13 TL
(had cruised in the sector which it was to have had. These shadows were) Tj T*
(ships going along the Italian coast.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(But another shadow, covered by the water, had been on watch for many) Tj T*
(days. It knew we were going by way of the Strait of Otranto. Advised by) Tj T*
(its accomplices, it awaited, motionless, the occasion for striking a) Tj T*
(decisive blow. For three nights, for four nights, the majestic cruisers) Tj T*
(passed too far from this shadow submarine, from this octopus with) Tj T*
(deadly tentacles. The moon, as it approached its full glory, became) Tj T*
(more and more luminous.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(During these splendid hours, when I had almost disrobed to feel the) Tj T*
(caresses of the night near me, the submarine saw approaching a slowly) Tj T*
(moving vessel, with four stacks and graceful outline. It made ready, as) Tj T*
(it had the night before and the night before that, and hoped that the) Tj T*
(ship?s present route would permit it to cast its death thrust.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(What pen could describe this drama in all its fullness?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(On the _Gambetta_, sailors and officers scanned this sea that was) Tj T*
(almost too bright; they had seen it raging or seething with billows,) Tj T*
(or tormented by the wind, or calmer than a sleeping eyelid. It was the) Tj T*
(ninth month! Flashes of lightning dazzled their eyes, and they moved,) Tj T*
(like the watchers on the _Waldeck-Rousseau_, in a confusion of gleams) Tj T*
(and darkness. It was the two hundredth night! They were weary. They had) Tj T*
(waited so long, they no longer expected anything. Their eyes met only) Tj T*
(illusion.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The submarine lay in wait in the bosom of the waves. It knew that) Tj T*
(some time or other its wonderful prey would pass within range of its) Tj T*
(torpedo. Through the lens of the periscope its commander saw the) Tj T*
(luminous circle where the moon danced, the surface of the mirrored) Tj T*
(water, and the phantoms which move in a night at sea. He heard on the) Tj T*
(submerged hull the lapping of the dark waves. All the sailors at their) Tj T*
(posts watched the gesture of his hand and the sound of his voice.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Suddenly this man?s heart began to beat as if it would burst. God of) Tj T*
(death, you were speaking in his ear! He had just seen in the funnel of) Tj T*
(his periscope two masts and four stacks. She rose in the midst of the) Tj T*
(lightning flashes, a phantom. Tense and still, the man asked himself if) Tj T*
(the vision would approach, or would vanish as on the preceding nights.) Tj T*
(She approached. She came, a vagabond, predestined, without knowing that) Tj T*
(a demon was plotting her death. With closed lips and moist hands, this) Tj T*
(man prepared his words. Twenty-five men watched him as if he were a) Tj T*
(destroying angel.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(At the given moment he said: ?Fire!?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The torpedo left the submarine like a breath in the water and as) Tj T*
(silently. For a few seconds, a few endless seconds, it rushed through) Tj T*
(the echoless water. Two flashes, three flashes, gleamed in the sky; the) Tj T*
(lookouts on the _Gambetta_ covered their faces with their hands. They) Tj T*
