(Without mourning or benediction they laid their bodies in the cemetery) Tj T*
(of the sea. From Admiral to midshipmen, all the officers are buried) Tj T*
(in this sea, at once so maternal and malevolent. The superhuman souls) Tj T*
(of these officers attempted the impossible. They wished to save the) Tj T*
(cruiser, and the cruiser went down. They wished to save the men, and it) Tj T*
(is not their fault that nearly eight hundred sailors perished.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(And then, according to that law of the sea which ordains that the) Tj T*
(officer shall wait until the last sailor is saved, they went down with) Tj T*
(their ship. The ignorant will criticize them, but they are wrong. If) Tj T*
(each Frenchman, in civil or military service, performs to the uttermost) Tj T*
(the task his country demands of him, his country, with a heave of her) Tj T*
(shoulders, will chase the Germans out of France.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Officers of the _Gambetta_, you have your place in the paradise of ?_la) Tj T*
(Revanche_.?) Tj T*
